      "body": "Rebased this fix onto `9fa9308e95` in `9b489e5a4c`; the branch now includes the required `MIN_BASE_SHA`. I reran 79 conversation tests and 3 subtests on CPU and confirmed the non-alternating-role regressions fail with current main's production code. The complete `pre-commit run --all-files` check also passes, including Rust formatting and Clippy.\n\nThe functional patch is unchanged by the rebase. Could a maintainer authorize baseline CI for this head with `/tag-and-rerun-ci` and complete the code-owner review?",
